\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00.Permissionless. Extends the pool instance TTL.\00\00\00\00\00\11bump_instance_ttl\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\f6Quote the LP minted (deposit) or burned (withdrawal) for a balance change, imbalance fee\0ataken into account.\0a\0a- `amounts`: amount added or removed for each coin, one entry per coin.\0a- `is_deposit`: `true` to add `amounts`, `false` to remove them.\00\00\00\00\00\11calc_token_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07amounts\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ais_deposit\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00kValue of one LP token: invariant `D \c2\b7 precision() / lp_supply`, a `precision()`-scaled fixed-point number.\00\00\00\00\11get_virtual_price\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\003Permissionless. Extends an LP holder's balance TTL.\00\00\00\00\13bump_lp_balance_ttl\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00|Withdraw accumulated `admin_balances` out to the Factory's fee receiver.\0a\0aPermissionless: anyone may trigger the withdrawal.\00\00\00\13withdraw_admin_fees\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\004Off-peg fee multiplier, scaled by `FEE_DENOMINATOR`.\00\00\00\15offpeg_fee_multiplier\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\d7Quote the amount of coin `i` received for burning `burn_amount` LP in a one-coin withdrawal,\0awithdrawal fee taken into account.\0a\0a- `burn_amount`: LP-token amount being redeemed.\0a- `i`: index of the coin to withdraw.\00\00\00\00\16calc_withdraw_one_coin\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bburn_amount\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01i\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\f5Withdraw a single coin `i` by burning LP, returning the coin amount paid out.\0a\0aThe burn shrinks the invariant pro-rata; the payout is the resulting drop in coin `i`,\0areduced by the single-coin withdrawal fee.\0a\0a- `caller`: authorizes the call and is charged the LP burn.\0a- `burn_amount`: LP-token amount being redeemed.\0a- `i`: index of the coin to withdraw.\0a- `min_received`: slippage floor on the coins out.\0a- `receiver`: paid the coins.\0aOpens missing SAC trustlines with the receiver's authorization.\00\00\00\00\00\00\19remove_liquidity_one_coin\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bburn_amount\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01i\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cmin_received\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08receiver\00\00\00\14\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\18Withdraw an explicit, possibly imbalanced `amounts`, returning the LP actually burned.\0a\0aThe part of the withdrawal that shifts the pool away from its current balance is charged the\0aimbalance fee, so an imbalanced exit burns more LP than a balanced one of the same value.\0a\0a- `caller`: authorizes the call and is charged the LP burn.\0a- `amounts`: amount of each coin to withdraw, one entry per coin.\0a- `max_burn`: slippage cap on the LP burned.\0a- `receiver`: paid the coins.\0aOpens missing SAC trustlines with the receiver's authorization.\00\00\00\1aremove_liquidity_imbalance\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07amounts\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08max_burn\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08receiver\00\00\00\14\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\eeAll immutable settings supplied when a pool is constructed.\0a\0aThis is the single argument to a pool's `__constructor`. It is shared by the Factory, which\0aserializes and authorizes the call, and by the pool, which validates and persists